      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day (some labeling allows up to 3,000 mg/day). This dose is about 5 times that. A single 4,250 mg dose is also in the range associated with severe lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **425 mg PO three times daily**, if the decimal or a digit was misplaced (this isn't a standard tablet strength, so 500 mg TID may be closer)\n- Another dose or frequency\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away. If 4,250 mg is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording your confirmation. I'd still recommend pharmacy review first."
      }
