       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. I know I offered to earlier, and I'm sorry to go back on that. 12,750 mg/day of metformin is about 5 times the maximum labeled dose. It has no therapeutic benefit at that level, and it carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and death. I can't find a clinical scenario where it's intended, and I can't undo it once it reaches the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or a lower starting dose if you'd rather titrate.\n- **Send this to pharmacy.** If there's a reason for this dose that I'm missing, the clinical pharmacist or your institution's high-alert override process is the right route. They can verify it independently.\n- **Check the intended dose.** If this might be a transcription or unit error, tell me the dose you meant and I'll enter it.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
